  "body": " Class Structure    Class is a combination of lecture time, and group work\/coding time.  Bring computer every day  Jupyter notebooks  Website exercises  Group exercises      Once a week, there will be a short check-in quiz on the last day we have class that week (unless otherwise announced), mostly consisting of multiple choice questions. This will be basic content related to lectures since the last class. Possible questions include checking on definitions, or basic understanding of major ideas.  10 points per quiz  Drop three lowest grades      Homeworks due approximately biweekly, midnight of the day marked in the schedule.  Drop lowest grade.   Sliding scale for later HW.     Three midterms  See schedule for dates.  Not cumulative         Basic Expectations     attend each class for the full 70 min duration    take detailed notes on, or beside, the skeleton slides provided.    complete the jupyter notebook in class.    read the assigned textbook chapters listed in the course schedule (on course website).    actively participate in group work and interactive Q\\&A sessions.    complete all homework assignments, quizzes, exams, and a semester project.      "
