  "body": "     What do the columns of predict_proba function below correspond to?    Check your answer on the first few entries.     probabilities = logreg.predict_proba(X_test) print(logreg.classes_) print(probabilities[:5]) ...     The probability columns follow the exact order in logreg.classes_ .    For each row, the predicted label should match the class associated with the largest probability.    Common error: Do not assume alphabetical or numeric order without checking classes_ ; the estimator records the authoritative order.    The three columns correspond, in logreg.classes_ order, to setosa , versicolor , and virginica . Each row sums to 1, and its largest entry determines the label returned by predict .   probabilities = logreg.predict_proba(X_test) print('Classes:', logreg.classes_) for i in range(5): print(i, probabilities[i], 'prediction:', Y_pred[i])     "
