  "body": "   Using the .predict function, what is the species predicted for the first five data points in X ? Which of these predicted values are the same as the original labels?    Call clf_tree.predict(X_df.iloc[:5]) and place the result next to y_df.iloc[:5] .    An elementwise comparison such as predicted == actual makes each match explicit.    Common error: Use the shuffled y_df with the same row order as X_df ; resetting or separately shuffling one object would misalign labels.     yhat = clf_tree.predict(X_df) print(yhat[:5]) # In this case, they are all predicted correctly. print(y_df[:5])     "
