  "body": "   Use whatever worked for you above to plot your decision tree.    Use tree.plot_tree with clf_pair and the two feature names used to fit it.    Set filled=True and a large figure size to make the class regions and thresholds readable.    Common error: Pass exactly two feature names— bill_length_mm and bill_depth_mm ; supplying every column name from X_df does not match this two-feature tree.     fig = plt.figure(figsize=(20, 14)) tree.plot_tree( clf_pair, feature_names=['bill_length_mm', 'bill_depth_mm'], class_names=clf_pair.classes_, filled=True, fontsize=12 ) plt.show()     "
